1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,480
Here are two beakers of acid, both at

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:06,160
0.10 moles per litre, with the same piece

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,920
of magnesium in each.

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:10,640
In hydrochloric acid it fizzes hard.

5
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:14,240
In acetic acid, also called ethanoic acid, the

6
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:16,720
acid in vinegar, it fizzes slowly.

7
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:20,880
Same concentration, same metal, so why the difference?

8
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:24,000
The answer is an equilibrium, and it comes

9
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:26,080
with a K that has its own name.

10
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,940
The bubbles are hydrogen gas, made when the

11
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:32,820
magnesium meets hydrogen ions, H plus.

12
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:37,060
In water, every hydrochloric acid molecule breaks into

13
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:39,940
ions, H plus and chloride.

14
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:44,260
Breaking into ions is called dissociating, or ionising,

15
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:46,900
and because it goes all the way, hydrochloric

16
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:49,220
acid is a strong acid.

17
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:52,260
Acetic acid molecules break apart too, but the

18
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:54,660
ions also join back up, and the two

19
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:58,340
directions balance while most molecules are still whole.

20
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:00,820
At this concentration only about one in a

21
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:03,060
hundred is split at any moment.

22
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:05,780
So the acetic acid has far fewer hydrogen

23
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:07,860
ions to meet the magnesium.

24
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:10,580
An acid that only partly ionises is a

25
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:11,460
weak acid.

26
00:01:12,667 --> 00:01:15,226
A balance between molecules and ions is an

27
00:01:15,347 --> 00:01:18,026
equilibrium, so it has a K, written the

28
00:01:18,107 --> 00:01:19,466
way you already know.

29
00:01:19,787 --> 00:01:22,506
Write any weak acid as H A, which

30
00:01:22,587 --> 00:01:25,466
splits into H plus and A minus.

31
00:01:25,707 --> 00:01:28,346
Products over reactants gives H plus times A

32
00:01:28,427 --> 00:01:30,026
minus, over H A.

33
00:01:30,667 --> 00:01:32,986
Every coefficient is one, so there are no

34
00:01:33,067 --> 00:01:33,626
powers.

35
00:01:34,267 --> 00:01:37,706
This K is called Ka, the acid dissociation

36
00:01:37,787 --> 00:01:40,186
constant, and the little a just says which

37
00:01:40,307 --> 00:01:41,786
kind of reaction it belongs to.

38
00:01:42,427 --> 00:01:44,506
It is not a new kind of constant:

39
00:01:44,587 --> 00:01:47,386
it follows every rule from the expressions video,

40
00:01:47,427 --> 00:01:49,466
and it changes only with temperature.

41
00:01:50,667 --> 00:01:52,826
You will also see the same reaction written

42
00:01:52,907 --> 00:01:56,426
with water: H A plus water makes H

43
00:01:56,507 --> 00:01:58,506
three O plus and A minus.

44
00:01:59,067 --> 00:02:01,226
H three O plus is just a hydrogen

45
00:02:01,307 --> 00:02:03,226
ion carried by a water molecule.

46
00:02:03,787 --> 00:02:05,866
So does water go into Ka?

47
00:02:06,427 --> 00:02:06,986
No.

48
00:02:07,227 --> 00:02:09,786
Water is the solvent, there is a huge,

49
00:02:09,867 --> 00:02:12,266
steady amount of it, so it stays out,

50
00:02:12,387 --> 00:02:14,146
just as in the expressions video.

51
00:02:14,427 --> 00:02:16,986
Ka is H three O plus times A

52
00:02:17,067 --> 00:02:19,706
minus, over H A, the same shape as

53
00:02:19,787 --> 00:02:20,426
before.

54
00:02:21,634 --> 00:02:23,873
Now read the size, the same way as

55
00:02:23,954 --> 00:02:24,993
any K.

56
00:02:25,074 --> 00:02:28,833
For acetic acid, Ka is 1.8 times ten

57
00:02:28,914 --> 00:02:30,273
to the minus five.

58
00:02:30,514 --> 00:02:32,913
A tiny K means a small top and

59
00:02:32,954 --> 00:02:35,913
a big bottom, so at equilibrium most of

60
00:02:35,954 --> 00:02:38,353
the acid is still whole molecules.

61
00:02:39,567 --> 00:02:43,166
Hydrofluoric acid has a Ka of 6.8 times

62
00:02:43,247 --> 00:02:45,886
ten to the minus four, nearly forty times

63
00:02:46,047 --> 00:02:46,446
bigger.

64
00:02:47,007 --> 00:02:50,526
At 0.10 moles per litre, about eight in

65
00:02:50,607 --> 00:02:53,086
a hundred of its molecules are split, against

66
00:02:53,247 --> 00:02:55,806
about one in a hundred for acetic acid.

67
00:02:55,887 --> 00:02:58,446
So the bigger the Ka, the stronger the

68
00:02:58,567 --> 00:02:59,646
weak acid.

69
00:03:00,127 --> 00:03:02,886
Ka is not the concentration of H plus,

70
00:03:03,007 --> 00:03:05,846
and it is not the pH: those also

71
00:03:06,047 --> 00:03:07,886
depend on how much acid you dissolved.

72
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:11,020
What about hydrochloric acid?

73
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:14,540
It ionises completely, so at equilibrium there are

74
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:17,500
essentially no H C L molecules left to

75
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:18,940
go on the bottom of the fraction.

76
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:21,260
We don't use a Ka value for a

77
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:22,140
strong acid.

78
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:24,780
We simply say it ionises completely.

79
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:27,820
Ka is the tool for weak acids, where

80
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:30,220
molecules and ions are both present.

81
00:03:31,434 --> 00:03:33,033
Bases work the same way.

82
00:03:33,514 --> 00:03:35,913
Ammonia, a gas that is dissolved in some

83
00:03:35,994 --> 00:03:39,353
household cleaners, reacts with water: it takes a

84
00:03:39,514 --> 00:03:42,233
hydrogen ion from a water molecule, making an

85
00:03:42,314 --> 00:03:45,673
ammonium ion and a hydroxide ion, O H

86
00:03:45,754 --> 00:03:46,553
minus.

87
00:03:46,874 --> 00:03:49,433
The ions also join back up, so this

88
00:03:49,514 --> 00:03:50,793
is an equilibrium too.

89
00:03:51,434 --> 00:03:53,993
Here water is a reactant, but it is

90
00:03:54,154 --> 00:03:56,473
still the solvent, so it stays out.

91
00:03:57,034 --> 00:04:01,113
The constant is Kb, the base dissociation constant:

92
00:04:01,194 --> 00:04:04,393
ammonium times hydroxide, over ammonia.

93
00:04:04,714 --> 00:04:07,993
For ammonia, Kb is 1.8 times ten to

94
00:04:08,034 --> 00:04:10,633
the minus five, so most of the ammonia

95
00:04:10,714 --> 00:04:13,193
stays as molecules, which makes it a weak

96
00:04:13,274 --> 00:04:13,913
base.

97
00:04:15,134 --> 00:04:17,053
One more, so you can see the pattern.

98
00:04:17,614 --> 00:04:21,133
A solid that barely dissolves, like silver chloride,

99
00:04:21,214 --> 00:04:23,053
sits in balance with its ions in the

100
00:04:23,214 --> 00:04:24,573
water around it.

101
00:04:24,694 --> 00:04:28,013
Silver chloride solid makes silver ions and chloride

102
00:04:28,094 --> 00:04:29,053
ions.

103
00:04:29,094 --> 00:04:31,053
The solid stays out, because it is a

104
00:04:31,214 --> 00:04:33,773
pure solid, so its K is just silver

105
00:04:33,854 --> 00:04:36,093
ions times chloride ions.

106
00:04:36,134 --> 00:04:38,813
It is called Ksp, and you will calculate

107
00:04:38,894 --> 00:04:40,333
with it in later videos.

108
00:04:41,534 --> 00:04:44,733
So here is a line to remember: Ka,

109
00:04:44,894 --> 00:04:48,093
Kb and Ksp are just K with a

110
00:04:48,174 --> 00:04:48,893
name tag.

111
00:04:49,374 --> 00:04:52,653
Write them the same way, products over reactants,

112
00:04:52,734 --> 00:04:54,693
with water and solids left out.

113
00:04:54,894 --> 00:04:57,053
And read them the same way: when you

114
00:04:57,254 --> 00:04:59,853
compare reactions of the same kind, a bigger

115
00:04:59,934 --> 00:05:02,333
value means the reaction goes further to the

116
00:05:02,414 --> 00:05:02,893
right.

117
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:05,020
Your turn.

118
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:08,580
Methanoic acid, the acid in ant stings, has

119
00:05:08,633 --> 00:05:11,060
a Ka of 1.8 times ten to the

120
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:12,500
minus four.

121
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:15,940
Hydrogen cyanide, H C N, has a Ka

122
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:19,380
of 6.2 times ten to the minus ten.

123
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:22,260
One: write the Ka expression for H C

124
00:05:22,340 --> 00:05:24,900
N plus water making H three O plus

125
00:05:25,060 --> 00:05:26,260
and C N minus.

126
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:30,060
Two: which is the stronger acid, and why?

127
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:31,620
Pause here to answer.

128
00:05:42,034 --> 00:05:42,433
One.

129
00:05:42,674 --> 00:05:47,073
Products over reactants, with water left out: Ka

130
00:05:47,234 --> 00:05:49,873
is H three O plus times C N

131
00:05:49,954 --> 00:05:52,353
minus, over H C N.

132
00:05:52,674 --> 00:05:54,673
If you put water on the bottom, take

133
00:05:54,714 --> 00:05:56,753
it out, because it is the solvent.

134
00:05:57,967 --> 00:05:58,566
Two.

135
00:05:58,767 --> 00:06:02,046
Methanoic acid is stronger, because its Ka is

136
00:06:02,087 --> 00:06:05,086
bigger, so at the same concentration more of

137
00:06:05,167 --> 00:06:08,246
its molecules are split into ions at equilibrium.

138
00:06:08,687 --> 00:06:11,966
If you picked hydrogen cyanide because 6.2 is

139
00:06:12,007 --> 00:06:14,606
bigger than 1.8, look at the powers of

140
00:06:14,767 --> 00:06:16,126
ten first.

141
00:06:16,207 --> 00:06:18,366
Ten to the minus four is far bigger

142
00:06:18,487 --> 00:06:20,926
than ten to the minus ten, so methanoic

143
00:06:21,007 --> 00:06:24,286
acid's Ka is about three hundred thousand times

144
00:06:24,367 --> 00:06:24,846
bigger.

145
00:06:26,067 --> 00:06:27,826
So when you meet an acid or a

146
00:06:27,907 --> 00:06:31,026
base in water, write its K exactly like

147
00:06:31,187 --> 00:06:35,266
any other: products over reactants, water left out.

148
00:06:35,507 --> 00:06:38,306
Call it Ka for an acid and Kb

149
00:06:38,387 --> 00:06:40,946
for a base, and read its size: at

150
00:06:41,027 --> 00:06:44,226
the same concentration, bigger means more split into

151
00:06:44,307 --> 00:06:44,866
ions.

152
